  "modified": "2026-09-21T03:24:44Z",
  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: out-of-bounds write in stab_xcoff_builtin_type\n     (binutils/stabs.c)\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2021-45078.patch: reject negative and out-of-range\n       XCOFF builtin type numbers instead of indexing info->xcoff_types with\n       them\n     - CVE-2021-45078\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: heap buffer overflow in\n     read_section_stabs_debugging_info (binutils/rddbg.c)\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2021-46174.patch: check the stab section holds a\n       whole number of entries before reading them\n     - CVE-2021-46174\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: heap buffer overflow in find_section_in_set\n     (binutils/readelf.c)\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2022-44840.patch: fill the shndx pool by scanning\n       it directly so each set stays NUL terminated for a crafted\n       .debug_cu_index\n     - CVE-2022-44840\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: out-of-bounds read in parse_module (bfd/vms-alpha.c)\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2022-47673_CVE-2023-25584.patch: sanity check VMS\n       debug record lengths and DST element sizes before reading them\n     - CVE-2022-47673\n     - CVE-2023-25584\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: NULL pointer dereference in compare_symbols\n     (binutils/objdump.c)\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2022-47695.patch: guard the section comparison\n       against symbols that have no section\n     - CVE-2022-47695\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: crash on an uninitialised asymbol from\n     bfd_mach_o_get_synthetic_symtab (bfd/mach-o.c)\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2022-47696.patch: initialise the_bfd on the\n       synthetic symbols so objdump can sort them\n     - CVE-2022-47696\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: NULL pointer dereference in elf_gc_sweep\n     (bfd/elflink.c)\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2025-5244.patch: skip the gc_mark propagation when\n       a section group has no first member\n     - CVE-2025-5244\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: NULL pointer dereference in debug_type_samep and\n     debug_write_type (binutils/debug.c)\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2025-5245.patch: handle enum types that carry no\n       name list\n     - CVE-2025-5245\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: NULL pointer dereference in process_relocs\n     (binutils/readelf.c)\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2025-69649.patch: do not walk the section headers\n       when the file has none\n     - CVE-2025-69649\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: out-of-bounds reads in xcoff_link_add_symbols\n     (bfd/xcofflink.c)\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-3441_CVE-2026-3442.patch: bound the XTY_LD\n       x_scnlen csect index by the symbol count rather than by the byte\n       offset into the symbol table, and range-check r_symndx before\n       indexing the symbol hashes\n     - CVE-2026-3441\n     - CVE-2026-3442\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: heap buffer overflow in xcoff_link_add_symbols\n     (bfd/xcofflink.c)\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-6846.patch: size the reloc_info array by the\n       highest section target_index\n     - CVE-2026-6846",
